The survey's lead on recommendation holds, and the search delay is a call-level slowdown, not a CPU problem. Two faults stand out, both with their effects reaching frontend.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "recommendation",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) AS n FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name = 'recommendation' GROUP BY 1,2 UNION ALL SELECT 'abnormal_' || service_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'recommendation' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Recommendation emits 697 server spans in normal period and none at all in the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT regexp_extract(message, '\"reason\":\"([A-Za-z]+)\"', 1) AS reason, regexp_extract(message, '\"name\":\"([^\"]+)\"', 1) AS objname, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE message LIKE '%recommendation-%' GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY n DESC", "claim": "Kubelet events show recommendation pod in BackOff and Failed (crash loop) during the incident, with no recovery event."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name = 'HTTP /recommendations' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Frontend /recommendations returns HTTP 500 in about 0.1 ms, 71 times, with no downstream recommendation work."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE message = 'Recommendation service failed' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Frontend logs 155 ERROR entries 'Recommendation service failed' during the abnormal window; none in normal."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) AS n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,1) AS p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'search' AND span_name = 'rate.Rate/GetRates' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Search's outgoing rate.Rate/GetRates client spans take about 1.8 s p50 versus about 1 ms normally."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) AS n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'rate' AND attr_span_kind = 'Server' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Rate's own server spans stay fast (p95 about 1.4 ms) while search's calls to it take about 2.6 s."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, count(*) AS n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,1) AS p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'search' AND attr_span_kind = 'Client' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Search's calls to geo stay fast (about 0.5 ms) while only its calls to rate are slow."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT service_name, metric, round(avg(value),4) AS av FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name = 'search' AND metric = 'container.cpu.usage' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Search container CPU is low during the incident (about 0.002), so the slowdown is not CPU saturation."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "recommendation",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name = 'HTTP /recommendations' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Frontend /recommendations requests fail with HTTP 500 because the recommendation backend is down."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, count(*) AS n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name = 'HTTP /hotels' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Frontend /hotels p95 rises to about 2 s, matching the slow search.Search/Nearby calls it makes."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

